From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -service_columns, room in the array
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-service_columns {every sites} puts an empty column `sites` sites wide
after every `every` storage columns. An array of placed standard cells
is full: a parent flow that buffers the long nets crossing it (repair
inserts wire buffers on the word selects and read bitlines) has no site
to put them on, and legalization fails. XiangShan's RobEntryFile,
352 words of 21 bits with 16 read and 8 write ports, dissolved into a
parent, left 1,230 such buffers overlapping without these columns. The
columns are inside the core, so -periphery unplaced keeps them in the
outline. Default: none, as before.

Tested: src/ram/test/service_columns_asap7.tcl.

Commit 15 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
